# Brahms' Lullaby, melody with chords (repertoire plan: brahms-lullaby). Brahms' Wiegenlied,
# Op. 49 No. 4, moved from E-flat major to G major, so the tune runs from the open string 3 (G)
# up to string 1 fret 3 (G), all in first position, with the octave leap from one G to the other
# in the second half. Played without words. You play the tune; the teacher plays the rocking
# accompaniment (bass note on beat 1, chord on beats 2 and 3) on G (320003), D7 (xx0212) and
# C (x32010). Then swap parts.
title: Brahms' Lullaby
id: brahms-lullaby
composer: Johannes Brahms
source: Wiegenlied (Cradle Song), Op. 49 No. 4 (1868), moved to G major; melody and accompaniment arranged for Sixstring Academy
arranger: Sixstring Academy
licence: Public domain (Brahms died in 1897); this arrangement is original to Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 3
tags: lullaby, waltz time, melody, octave leap
tempo: 72
time: 3/4
key: G
pickup: q

track: Melody
role: lead
